family_id|category|product|complaint|paraphrase|attempted|diagnostic|cause|action|verification|severity|avoid
BB01|broadband_outage|fibre_broadband|The optical box has a red LOS light and every device is offline. Restarting did nothing.|No internet anywhere at home; the fibre unit still shows loss of signal after a reboot.|Restarted the ONT once; no change.|Agent optical test reports no received signal; account is active.|External fibre break.|Raise a fibre repair job; an authorized technician repairs the external span.|Simulated follow-up: optical signal restored and wired browsing works.|high|Do not factory-reset the router or tell the customer to handle exposed fibre.
BB02|broadband_outage|fibre_broadband|The fibre lights are normal but neither my wired desktop nor Wi-Fi devices can browse. The router says authentication failed.|Internet stopped on all devices although the optical link looks healthy; the connection page reports a sign-in failure.|Checked a wired device and restarted the router once.|Optical signal is healthy; the subscriber session is rejected after an account migration.|Stale access-session provisioning.|Authorized provisioning team corrects the subscriber session mapping and reconnects it.|Simulated follow-up: session authenticates and both wired and wireless browsing work.|high|Do not ask the customer to share account passwords in a ticket.
BB03|broadband_outage|fibre_broadband|All the flats on my street lost fibre service together. Our building's shared office cannot get online either.|Neighbours and I went offline at the same moment, and the shared office has no connection.|Checked with neighbours; power and local router lights are normal.|Provider incident record confirms a regional aggregation outage affecting multiple buildings.|Regional aggregation equipment failure.|Link affected lines to the major incident; network operations restore the failed equipment and provide a status update.|Simulated follow-up: incident closes after regional service checks pass.|critical|Do not promise a restoration time before network operations supplies one.
BB04|broadband_outage|fibre_broadband|Internet stopped just after my address transfer completed. The ONT light is green but the WAN stays disconnected.|Since moving my service, the fibre seems connected but my router cannot establish an internet session.|Verified cables are seated and power-cycled once.|New-address order references the previous ONT serial; the installed ONT is absent from provisioning.|Incorrect ONT association after relocation.|Authorized provisioning staff validate the installed device against the order and correct its association.|Simulated follow-up: the relocated line establishes a session and passes browsing checks.|high|Do not reprovision a different subscriber's ONT.
ID01|intermittent_broadband|fibre_broadband|The connection drops on my wired computer too, mostly when it rains. Restarting the router did not help.|Wet weather knocks out both Ethernet and Wi-Fi at home even after a restart.|Restarted once and compared wired with wireless.|Optical loss events align with rain; technician finds moisture at an external joint.|Moisture-damaged external optical joint.|Dispatch an authorized technician to repair and seal the damaged joint.|Simulated follow-up: no optical loss events during the next wet-weather observation.|high|Do not treat this as Wi-Fi interference or recommend repeated reboots.
ID02|intermittent_broadband|fibre_broadband|Every evening the internet pauses on all devices, including my wired laptop. The optical light remains normal.|Our entire connection stalls during busy evening hours while the fibre indicator stays steady.|Tested Ethernet and stopped local downloads; stalls continue.|Line stays synchronized; provider monitoring shows peak-hour congestion on the access segment.|Congested access segment.|Network operations rebalance capacity and monitor the affected segment during peak hours.|Simulated follow-up: peak-hour packet loss subsides and calls stay connected.|high|Do not promise that a Wi-Fi channel change will repair provider congestion.
ID03|intermittent_broadband|fibre_broadband|The internet disconnects for a minute at almost the same interval on Ethernet and Wi-Fi, with no change in the fibre light.|All devices lose access periodically, but the ONT never loses optical signal.|Restarted the router and recorded three disconnect times.|Gateway logs show session renewals failing against a stale lease record.|Access-session renewal failure.|Authorized access team clears the stale lease and applies the validated renewal configuration.|Simulated follow-up: multiple renewal cycles complete without interruption.|high|Do not diagnose a broken optical cable without optical fault evidence.
ID04|intermittent_broadband|fibre_broadband|The ONT flickers off briefly and all devices lose internet. The router stays powered on.|My fibre box keeps losing power for a moment while the separate router remains lit.|Checked the outlet with another appliance; outlet is stable.|Authorized technician reproduces voltage drops with the ONT power adapter.|Failing ONT power adapter.|Replace the adapter with the provider-approved matching unit.|Simulated follow-up: ONT power and the internet session remain stable through observation.|high|Do not suggest opening the adapter or using an incompatible supply.
SP01|slow_broadband|fibre_broadband|My upgrade to 300 Mbps completed, but repeated wired tests stop around the old 100 Mbps rate.|Ethernet speed has not changed since I upgraded my plan, even with other devices idle.|Used a capable wired device and paused background traffic.|Subscription is 300 Mbps but provisioning retains the 100 Mbps profile.|Old speed profile after plan upgrade.|Authorized provisioning team applies the purchased speed profile and repeats a wired test.|Simulated follow-up: wired throughput is consistent with the updated profile under test conditions.|medium|Do not promise exact advertised throughput on every device.
SP02|slow_broadband|fibre_broadband|Downloads on my Ethernet desktop are much slower than on another wired computer. My desktop link says 100 Mbps.|One cabled PC is stuck at a low rate but a second wired machine is fast.|Compared two wired devices and checked link speed.|Moving the affected PC to a known-good cable negotiates a gigabit link.|Damaged Ethernet cable limiting link negotiation.|Replace the damaged cable with a compatible tested cable.|Simulated follow-up: the PC negotiates the expected link rate and repeat transfers improve.|medium|Do not change the subscription or blame the access network when another wired device performs normally.
SP03|slow_broadband|fibre_broadband|Both of my wired computers become slow only in the evening. During the morning the same speed test is normal.|Ethernet throughput collapses at busy hours even with Wi-Fi switched off.|Disabled local downloads and repeated timed wired tests.|Provider utilization correlates with reduced peak-hour throughput; physical line tests pass.|Peak-hour backhaul saturation.|Network operations expand or rebalance backhaul capacity and verify peak-hour throughput.|Simulated follow-up: repeated evening tests improve after the capacity change.|medium|Do not attribute wired-only tests to wireless signal strength.
SP04|slow_broadband|fibre_broadband|All transfers slow down whenever our backup computer is running. Pausing its backup makes the connection normal.|The whole house feels slow during cloud uploads, but stopping that job fixes it temporarily.|Paused the backup and compared throughput before and after.|Gateway counters show the backup saturating the uplink; access profile is correct.|Local upload saturation.|Schedule the backup outside working hours or apply a supported upload limit.|Simulated follow-up: video calls and browsing remain usable while the limited backup runs.|medium|Do not raise a line-repair visit without evidence of a line fault.
WF01|wifi_connectivity|home_wifi|Wi-Fi is good beside the router but almost unusable upstairs. My wired computer is fine.|Only the upstairs rooms lose wireless access; Ethernet and the room near the router work.|Compared rooms and a wired device.|Coverage survey shows weak signal behind several walls; WAN is stable.|Insufficient indoor wireless coverage.|Reposition the access point safely; assess a supported mesh node if coverage remains inadequate.|Simulated follow-up: signal and browsing improve in the previously affected room.|medium|Do not label this a broadband outage or promise coverage without checking placement.
WF02|wifi_connectivity|home_wifi|Wi-Fi slows down in the apartment every evening but Ethernet stays fast, even at that time.|Only wireless devices struggle at night; my wired laptop keeps its normal speed.|Compared simultaneous wired and wireless tests.|Wireless survey shows a crowded channel; wired tests and WAN counters are normal.|Wireless channel contention.|Choose an appropriate supported channel or band after checking device compatibility.|Simulated follow-up: wireless retries decrease and the evening test improves.|medium|Do not blame provider backhaul when concurrent Ethernet tests are normal.
WF03|wifi_connectivity|home_wifi|My smart plug cannot see the new Wi-Fi network, although my laptop connects without trouble.|The new router works for my computer, but a 2.4 GHz-only appliance cannot join it.|Confirmed the appliance supports only 2.4 GHz.|Router is advertising only a band the appliance does not support.|Client and wireless-band incompatibility.|Enable a supported 2.4 GHz network using an appropriate security mode and reconnect the appliance.|Simulated follow-up: appliance connects while existing devices retain access.|low|Do not disable Wi-Fi security to make the device connect.
WF04|wifi_connectivity|home_wifi|Since I renamed Wi-Fi, one laptop keeps saying the password is incorrect while my phone connects.|A single computer will not join after the network-name change; other devices are online.|Verified the current credentials through the router's approved local interface.|Laptop retains an old saved wireless profile; other clients authenticate.|Stale client wireless profile.|Remove the obsolete saved profile on that device and reconnect using the current credentials locally.|Simulated follow-up: laptop joins and obtains an address.|low|Do not collect or print the customer's Wi-Fi password.
HW01|router_ont_hardware|router|The router has no lights, but the wall socket works with a lamp.|My router is completely dead even though the outlet has power.|Checked the outlet and the external power connector.|Authorized hardware check identifies a failed approved power adapter.|Router power adapter failure.|Replace with the approved adapter matching the device requirements.|Simulated follow-up: router powers on and passes a connection check.|high|Do not open a mains adapter or use an arbitrary substitute.
HW02|router_ont_hardware|router|The router keeps restarting after its update. Internet was fine before the update began.|A firmware update ended and now the router never gets past its startup cycle.|Performed one controlled restart; boot loop persists.|Authorized support reads a failed firmware validation event for this device model.|Failed firmware update.|Authorized support follows the model-specific recovery procedure with a verified firmware image.|Simulated follow-up: router boots normally and configuration checks pass.|high|Do not provide generic flashing commands or download firmware from an unverified source.
HW03|router_ont_hardware|router|The router gets unusually hot in a closed cabinet and shuts down, then works after cooling.|My gateway turns off after warming up; it is inside a cupboard.|Powered it down and moved it to a ventilated position.|Device still overheats in a safe ventilated location; authorized inspection flags a hardware fault.|Internal router thermal fault.|Stop using the faulty unit and arrange approved hardware replacement.|Simulated follow-up: replacement remains stable under normal operating conditions.|high|Do not tell the customer to open the case or continue using a visibly damaged unit.
HW04|router_ont_hardware|router|Every LAN socket works except one; a known-good cable and laptop fail only in that socket.|A single Ethernet port on the router is dead while the other ports work.|Swapped the cable and device across ports.|Port diagnostics confirm a physical port fault; service and other ports are healthy.|Failed router LAN port.|Use a working port temporarily and arrange a supported repair or replacement.|Simulated follow-up: replacement port negotiates normally with the tested device.|medium|Do not reset all service settings for an isolated confirmed port fault.
MC01|mobile_coverage|mobile|Signal disappears inside my apartment but comes back outside. Another phone on the same network behaves the same way.|Calls and data have weak reception indoors, yet both phones work in the street.|Compared indoors and outdoors on two devices.|No area outage; indoor attenuation is reproducible on multiple devices.|Building-related coverage attenuation.|Assess supported Wi-Fi calling and record the location for coverage review.|Simulated follow-up: supported Wi-Fi calling works indoors; outdoor coverage remains normal.|medium|Do not promise a new tower or request precise location in public logs.
MC02|mobile_coverage|mobile|Several neighbours and I suddenly have no mobile signal outdoors either.|Phones on this network all lost reception across our block at once.|Checked another device and an outdoor location.|Network incident confirms an affected serving site.|Serving-site outage.|Associate the reports with the network incident and provide the confirmed status; operations restore the site.|Simulated follow-up: test devices register after site restoration.|high|Do not keep resetting each customer's phone during a confirmed site outage.
MC03|mobile_coverage|mobile|My phone has no service after I manually selected a network on a trip. Other phones here work.|Back home my handset will not register, but reception is normal for everyone else.|Restarted once; the manually selected network remains configured.|Device is locked to an unavailable operator; account and SIM are active.|Manual operator selection left enabled.|Return network selection to automatic using the supported device settings.|Simulated follow-up: handset registers with the home network.|medium|Do not replace an active SIM before checking operator selection.
MC04|mobile_coverage|mobile|My handset loses signal everywhere, but the same SIM works in another compatible phone.|Reception is poor only on this device; moving its SIM to a second handset fixes it.|Cross-tested the SIM in a compatible unlocked phone.|Known-good SIM also fails in the original handset; local network checks pass.|Handset radio fault.|Refer the customer to authorized device support after preserving the cross-test findings.|Simulated follow-up: repaired handset registers normally.|medium|Do not claim a telecom network repair will fix confirmed handset hardware.
VC01|voice_call_failure|mobile_voice|Mobile data works, but every outgoing call fails. Incoming calls still arrive.|I can browse and receive calls, but dialing any normal number fails.|Tested more than one destination number.|Account has an unintended outgoing-call restriction; voice registration is otherwise healthy.|Incorrect outgoing-call barring.|Authorized account staff verify identity and remove the unintended restriction.|Simulated follow-up: outgoing test calls to two normal numbers connect.|high|Do not remove a legitimate customer-requested restriction without authorization.
VC02|voice_call_failure|mobile_voice|Calls disconnect when I move between rooms, but data continues and stationary calls are better.|Voice drops during movement even though I still have mobile internet.|Compared stationary and moving calls at the same location.|Network traces show a voice handover failure between serving cells.|Voice handover configuration fault.|Radio operations correct the affected handover configuration and retest.|Simulated follow-up: calls continue through the previously failing route.|high|Do not infer that data service proves voice handovers are healthy.
VC03|voice_call_failure|mobile_voice|My new compatible phone has fast data but calls fail immediately. The same SIM could call in my old phone.|Browsing works on the replacement handset but voice calls never connect.|Confirmed device compatibility and restarted once.|Voice-over-LTE registration is missing for the line despite compatible hardware.|IMS voice provisioning missing.|Authorized provisioning team restores the supported voice service profile.|Simulated follow-up: IMS registers and normal incoming and outgoing calls work.|high|Do not instruct the customer to place emergency calls as a test.
VC04|voice_call_failure|mobile_voice|Incoming calls go straight to another number, but I can make outgoing calls.|People cannot reach my phone because their calls are being forwarded elsewhere.|Checked that the handset is reachable and not in airplane mode.|Account inspection confirms an unintended forwarding rule.|Unexpected call-forwarding configuration.|After identity verification, review and remove only the unwanted forwarding setting.|Simulated follow-up: an ordinary incoming test call rings the handset.|medium|Do not disclose the forwarding destination before identity verification.
MD01|mobile_data|mobile_data|Calls and texts work after I changed phones, but mobile data does not. Wi-Fi works.|My SIM can call in the new handset, yet apps load only on wireless internet.|Enabled mobile data and restarted once.|Device access-point settings differ from the provider-approved profile; allowance is available.|Incorrect APN configuration.|Restore the approved APN using the provider's authenticated device guide.|Simulated follow-up: browsing works with Wi-Fi disabled.|medium|Do not invent APN credentials or send the customer to an unofficial settings site.
MD02|mobile_data|mobile_data|Data became very slow after I used most of my allowance, while calls still work.|Internet on my phone slowed sharply near the end of the billing cycle.|Checked usage in the authenticated account portal.|Usage has reached the plan's documented fair-use threshold; network diagnostics pass.|Plan-based data throttling.|Explain the fictional plan's displayed limit and available authorized options without changing the plan automatically.|Simulated follow-up: customer chooses an approved option and service matches its stated terms.|medium|Do not sell or apply an add-on without consent.
MD03|mobile_data|mobile_data|My dual-SIM phone tries to use the inactive SIM for internet. Calls on my active line work.|There is no cellular browsing even though the phone has an active subscription in the other slot.|Checked which SIM is selected for mobile data.|Device data preference points to the inactive subscription.|Wrong default data SIM.|Select the customer's active data subscription in the device settings with consent.|Simulated follow-up: mobile browsing works on the intended subscription.|low|Do not enable paid roaming on the other SIM as a workaround.
MD04|mobile_data|mobile_data|Mobile data stopped after a plan change, but voice and SMS still work on this line.|Only cellular internet failed when my package changed; calls were unaffected.|Restarted once and verified mobile data is enabled.|Account migration omitted the packet-data entitlement; device APN is correct.|Missing data entitlement after plan change.|Authorized provisioning team restores the purchased data entitlement.|Simulated follow-up: a packet-data session establishes and browsing succeeds.|medium|Do not treat correct device settings as evidence that account provisioning is complete.
SA01|sim_esim_activation|sim|My replacement physical SIM stays inactive. The serial on the order does not match the card I received.|The delivered SIM cannot activate and its printed identifier differs from my order.|Compared the order and delivered card through the secure support process.|Order is bound to a different SIM identifier; identity is verified.|SIM identifier mismatch.|Authorized activation staff reconcile the order and correct the approved SIM association.|Simulated follow-up: the delivered SIM activates and normal service checks pass.|high|Do not post full SIM identifiers in logs or activate an unverified line.
SA02|sim_esim_activation|esim|I scanned my eSIM code once on another phone and it now says already used on this one.|Moving my eSIM to a new device fails because the previous download code is no longer usable.|Confirmed the old activation code was previously consumed.|Activation system marks the profile token as used; transfer authorization is verified.|Consumed eSIM activation token.|Follow the authenticated eSIM transfer process and issue a replacement profile if eligible.|Simulated follow-up: the approved new device registers on the transferred line.|high|Do not request the activation QR code in an open ticket or duplicate active credentials.
SA03|sim_esim_activation|sim|The new SIM arrived, but activation says identity verification is still pending.|My line cannot go live because the order is waiting for verification, not because of signal.|Checked activation status in the account portal.|Required verification task is incomplete in the authorized onboarding workflow.|Pending activation verification.|Direct the customer to the secure verification workflow and resume activation after approval.|Simulated follow-up: approved verification allows provisioning to complete.|medium|Do not bypass verification or request identity documents through an unapproved channel.
SA04|sim_esim_activation|esim|My phone cannot add the eSIM profile even though my order is active; it reports the feature is unsupported.|The activation screen is unavailable on this handset despite an active eSIM order.|Checked the exact device variant against the supported-device list.|This device variant does not support the ordered eSIM capability.|Unsupported device for eSIM.|Explain supported-device options or offer an eligible physical-SIM exchange through the normal process.|Simulated follow-up: service activates on a supported device or approved replacement SIM.|medium|Do not repeatedly issue new eSIM codes for incompatible hardware.
NP01|number_porting|mobile|My number transfer was rejected because the details do not match the old provider's account.|The port has not started; the rejection mentions account information.|Reviewed the rejection reason without resubmitting.|Donor account details differ from the verified port request.|Port-request identity mismatch.|Correct only verified request details through the secure porting workflow and resubmit with consent.|Simulated follow-up: donor accepts the corrected request.|medium|Do not guess account identifiers or repeatedly submit conflicting requests.
NP02|number_porting|mobile|The transfer date is still tomorrow, but I expected the new SIM to work today. My old line still works.|My number has not moved yet; the scheduled port window has not arrived.|Checked the confirmed transfer window.|Port order is accepted and scheduled; no failure is recorded.|Port still within the accepted schedule.|Explain the recorded window and keep the old service available until the scheduled transfer completes.|Simulated follow-up: number moves during the recorded window.|low|Do not cancel the old line prematurely or invent a guaranteed completion time.
NP03|number_porting|mobile|After my number moved, outgoing calls work but some people calling me reach an error.|The new SIM can dial out, but callers from another network cannot reach my ported number.|Collected ordinary failed-call timestamps and originating networks.|Post-port routing is incomplete for a subset of originating networks.|Incomplete inter-operator routing after port.|Porting operations correct the routing records and test from affected networks.|Simulated follow-up: calls from the affected networks reach the ported line.|high|Do not advise another port request for a routing repair.
NP04|number_porting|mobile|My transfer request expired before the new provider completed it. The old SIM still works.|The port authorization is no longer valid, and my number remains with the previous network.|Checked the expiry and current service state.|Order cannot proceed with the expired authorization.|Expired port authorization.|Guide the verified customer through obtaining a new valid authorization and updating the existing order.|Simulated follow-up: updated authorization is accepted without an unintended second order.|medium|Do not create duplicate port orders or deactivate the working line.
SM01|sms_otp|mobile_sms|Normal messages arrive but one bank's login codes never do. Other verification messages arrive.|Only a particular sender's one-time codes are missing; ordinary SMS still works.|Checked the sender and approximate message times without sharing any code.|Network trace shows no message submission from the affected sender; other SMS delivers.|Sender-side OTP submission failure.|Provide trace findings and refer the customer to the sender's official support channel.|Simulated follow-up: sender fixes its submission and a new verification message arrives.|medium|Never request or repeat the customer's OTP.
SM02|sms_otp|mobile_sms|I can receive texts but cannot send any, even to ordinary mobile numbers.|Outgoing SMS fails to every contact while incoming texts continue.|Tried two ordinary recipients and restarted once.|Messaging profile contains an invalid service-center configuration.|Incorrect SMS service-center provisioning.|Authorized support restores the provider-approved messaging configuration.|Simulated follow-up: ordinary outgoing test messages deliver.|medium|Do not invent service-center numbers or use a paid shortcode to test.
SM03|sms_otp|mobile_sms|Since changing phones, messages from one contact are missing, but other people can text me.|A single sender's messages do not appear on my new handset.|Checked the handset's blocked and spam folders.|The sender is blocked locally; network delivery receipts are successful.|Local message filtering.|With consent, remove the unintended block or adjust the device's supported filtering setting.|Simulated follow-up: a new ordinary message from that sender is visible.|low|Do not disable all spam protection or expose message contents in logs.
SM04|sms_otp|mobile_sms|After porting, calls work but no text messages arrive from any network.|Voice is fine on my transferred number, yet incoming SMS is completely missing.|Tested ordinary SMS from two different networks.|SMS routing remains associated with the donor after voice routing completed.|Incomplete SMS routing after port.|Messaging and porting operations update the SMS routing and verify delivery.|Simulated follow-up: ordinary messages arrive from both test networks.|high|Do not request private verification codes as diagnostic evidence.
RM01|roaming|mobile_roaming|I am abroad with an active roaming pack; calls work but the account page says data roaming is disabled.|My travel package is present, but cellular internet is barred at account level.|Confirmed the pack and device roaming settings.|Roaming-data entitlement is disabled on the account despite the eligible pack.|Account-level roaming-data restriction.|After authentication and consent, apply the eligible roaming-data entitlement.|Simulated follow-up: a roaming data session establishes on a supported partner.|medium|Do not enable chargeable services without confirming pack coverage and consent.
RM02|roaming|mobile_roaming|My phone attached to a network abroad but has no data. Another listed partner is available.|Travel data fails on the current operator even though my pack covers this country.|Checked the current operator and package coverage.|Selected network is not a supported data partner for the fictional plan.|Unsupported roaming partner selection.|Guide selection of a supported available partner using the current approved partner list.|Simulated follow-up: browsing works on the eligible partner network.|medium|Do not assume every available network is included in the pack.
RM03|roaming|mobile_roaming|I purchased a travel pack, but its start date is tomorrow and I arrived today.|My roaming package is visible but not yet active on the date of my arrival.|Checked the pack's displayed validity dates.|Purchase succeeded; service date has not started.|Roaming pack validity has not begun.|Explain the recorded validity and authorized change options; obtain consent before any paid change.|Simulated follow-up: customer-approved date change activates eligible data service.|medium|Do not automatically backdate coverage or promise refunds.
RM04|roaming|mobile_roaming|The pack covers my destination, but I have already used all its data. Calls still work.|Roaming internet stopped after the travel allowance was exhausted.|Checked remaining allowance in the authenticated portal.|Roaming allowance is exhausted with no active additional entitlement.|Exhausted roaming data allowance.|Explain remaining service and approved top-up choices without purchasing on the customer's behalf.|Simulated follow-up: a customer-approved top-up restores eligible data.|medium|Do not silently switch to out-of-bundle charging.
BD01|billing_dispute|billing|My statement shows two completed payments for the same invoice, not one pending card hold.|The same monthly invoice was paid twice and both transactions settled.|Compared the two settled references in the secure billing portal.|Ledger confirms duplicate settled payments against one invoice.|Duplicate settled payment.|Authorized billing staff reconcile the ledger and initiate the approved duplicate-payment adjustment.|Simulated follow-up: adjustment appears in the ledger and is communicated to the customer.|medium|Do not refund a pending authorization or promise a universal refund deadline.
BD02|billing_dispute|billing|An entertainment add-on appears on my bill, but I do not remember authorizing it.|My invoice includes an extra service that I did not request.|Identified the disputed line item without changing the subscription.|Audit trail has no valid consent record for the add-on.|Unsupported add-on charge.|Billing staff investigate consent, remove the unsupported charge through policy, and document the decision.|Simulated follow-up: corrected invoice excludes the unsupported add-on.|medium|Do not cancel unrelated services or assume every disputed charge is invalid.
BD03|billing_dispute|billing|My first invoice after changing plans is higher and contains part-month entries for both plans.|The new bill includes old and new package dates, and I cannot understand the total.|Compared invoice dates with the plan-change date.|Ledger shows correct non-overlapping prorated periods and no duplicate charge.|Valid prorated billing misunderstood.|Explain the dated line items and calculation; retain the valid charges unless new evidence shows an error.|Simulated follow-up: customer understands the calculation; no adjustment is posted.|low|Do not issue a credit merely because the customer is angry.
BD04|billing_dispute|billing|I cancelled a service before the invoice period, but the next bill still includes it.|The cancelled subscription is still being charged after its recorded end date.|Checked the cancellation confirmation and charged period.|Billing continued beyond the confirmed effective cancellation date.|Cancellation not synchronized to billing.|Authorized billing staff align the end date and adjust only the unsupported period.|Simulated follow-up: corrected ledger and next invoice reflect the cancellation.|medium|Do not erase valid charges incurred before the cancellation date.
PR01|payment_restoration|billing|My payment is settled in the portal, but my broadband still shows suspended for nonpayment.|I have a completed payment receipt and service remains barred.|Checked that the receipt is settled, not pending.|Ledger is paid; service-restoration event failed to reach provisioning.|Missed restoration event after payment.|Authorized staff reconcile the paid status and resend the approved restoration event.|Simulated follow-up: service becomes active and normal browsing resumes.|high|Do not ask the customer to pay twice.
PR02|payment_restoration|billing|My bank shows a pending payment, while the provider still says unpaid and my service is paused.|The money appears reserved at my bank, but no settled payment is visible on the account.|Checked transaction status in both secure systems.|Payment is an authorization only; provider has no settlement confirmation.|Payment not yet settled.|Explain the pending status and approved payment-support route without falsely marking the account paid.|Simulated follow-up: settlement later arrives and normal restoration proceeds.|high|Do not claim that a pending bank hold proves the invoice is paid.
PR03|payment_restoration|billing|I paid using the reference for my old account. My current line remains suspended.|The payment completed, but it landed against my previous subscription.|Compared masked account references through authenticated support.|Ledger identifies a settled payment on the wrong customer-owned account.|Payment allocated to the wrong account.|Authorized billing staff verify ownership and follow the approved reallocation procedure.|Simulated follow-up: payment is assigned correctly and eligible service is restored.|high|Do not move funds across unverified accounts.
PR04|payment_restoration|billing|The bill is paid, but the portal says the line is suspended for a separate account review.|Payment succeeded, yet the service restriction is not described as a billing hold.|Confirmed the settled invoice and displayed restriction reason.|Restriction belongs to an authorized account-review workflow rather than collections.|Non-billing restriction after payment.|Route to the authorized account-review team and explain that payment alone cannot clear this restriction.|Simulated follow-up: approved review clears the restriction; no billing override was used.|high|Do not bypass security or account-review controls to restore service.
TV01|iptv|iptv|Live TV buffers over Wi-Fi but works when I connect the box by Ethernet.|The television stream stutters wirelessly, while a wired test on the same box is smooth.|Compared Ethernet with Wi-Fi on the set-top box.|Box and service are healthy; wireless link shows loss during buffering.|Weak wireless link to the IPTV box.|Use the supported wired connection or improve wireless placement after a coverage check.|Simulated follow-up: playback stays stable on the tested connection.|medium|Do not change billing entitlements for a demonstrated local link problem.
TV02|iptv|iptv|Only channels in my newly purchased TV package show not authorized. Existing channels play normally.|My new channel bundle is billed, but its channels remain locked while old ones work.|Verified package purchase in the portal.|Billing has the package but the set-top-box entitlement has not synchronized.|Missing IPTV package entitlement.|Authorized provisioning staff synchronize the purchased channel entitlement.|Simulated follow-up: newly entitled channels play without changing other packages.|medium|Do not unlock channels the customer has not purchased.
TV03|iptv|iptv|The TV shows no picture even in the set-top box menu, but the box's network light is normal.|There is a blank screen before any streaming starts; other internet services work.|Selected the correct TV input and tested another HDMI cable.|Known-good cable restores the local menu; network and stream checks pass.|Faulty HDMI cable.|Replace the faulty display cable with a compatible cable.|Simulated follow-up: menus and channels display normally.|medium|Do not confuse absence of a local display signal with internet buffering.
TV04|iptv|iptv|One live channel fails on two boxes and on the provider app; other channels work.|A particular channel is unavailable across devices even though the rest of TV works.|Compared the affected channel across devices and checked another channel.|Provider incident confirms a failed source feed for that channel.|Channel-specific source-feed outage.|Link the report to the content incident and provide confirmed updates while operations restore the feed.|Simulated follow-up: affected channel plays on both devices after feed restoration.|medium|Do not factory-reset customer devices for a confirmed shared content outage.
